{
  "id": "chapter-06",
  "number": 6,
  "title": "Strings: Joining and Templates",
  "summary": "Build text from pieces using + and the cleaner backtick style.",
  "kicker": "Chapter 6",
  "heading": "Strings: Joining and Templates",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "joining-with-plus",
      "title": "Joining text with +",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A string is just text. To build a bigger string from smaller pieces, you can glue them together with the <code>+</code> sign. This is called concatenation."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "label": "Joining",
          "code": "const name = \"Asha\";\n\"Hello \" + name + \"!\"; // \"Hello Asha!\""
        },
        {
          "type": "run",
          "rows": 8,
          "code": "<p id=\"out\"></p>\n\n<script>\n  const name = \"Asha\";\n  const age = 20;\n  document.getElementById(\"out\").textContent =\n    \"Hello \" + name + \", age \" + age;\n</script>"
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "url": "https://javascript.info/string",
          "label": "More on javascript.info"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "template-literals",
      "title": "Template literals (backticks)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "All those <code>+</code> signs get messy fast. Instead, you can wrap text in backticks <code>``</code> and drop values straight in with <code>${ }</code>. It reads much more naturally."
        },
        {
          "type": "compare",
          "cards": [
            {
              "title": "With +",
              "code": "\"Hello \" + name + \", age \" + age"
            },
            {
              "title": "With ` `",
              "code": "`Hello ${name}, age ${age}`"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "run",
          "rows": 8,
          "code": "<p id=\"out\"></p>\n\n<script>\n  const name = \"Asha\";\n  const age = 20;\n  document.getElementById(\"out\").textContent = `Hello ${name}, age ${age}`;\n</script>"
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "Angular's <code>{{ name }}</code> in templates is the same idea — drop a value right into your text."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "strings-recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "A string is text, written in quotes.",
            "<code>+</code> joins strings together.",
            "Backticks with <code>${ }</code> are a cleaner way to mix text and values.",
            "This is the same idea as Angular's <code>{{ }}</code>."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "group": "JavaScript"
}
